#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:86
msgid "When Proportional Fonts Are Acceptable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:88
msgid ""
"Large title text (font_size >= 48) with short strings (1-3 words) can use"
" proportional fonts without visible kerning issues. For anything else — "
"labels, descriptions, multi-word text, small sizes — use monospace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:90
msgid "Font Availability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:92
msgid "**macOS**: Menlo (pre-installed), SF Mono"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:93
msgid "**Linux**: DejaVu Sans Mono (pre-installed), Liberation Mono"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:94
msgid "**Cross-platform**: JetBrains Mono (install from jetbrains.com)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:96
msgid ""
"`\"Menlo\"` is the safest default — pre-installed on macOS, and Linux "
"systems fall back to DejaVu Sans Mono."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:98
msgid "Fine-Grained Text Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:100
msgid ""
"`Text()` does not support `letter_spacing` or kerning parameters. For "
"fine control, use `MarkupText` with Pango attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:113
msgid "Minimum Font Size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_visual-design.md:115
msgid ""
"`font_size=18` is the minimum for readable text at any resolution. Below "
"18, characters become blurry at `-ql` and barely readable even at `-qh`."
msgstr ""

